   "daf": "34a",
   "sentenceId": 5,
   "he": "שִׁילֵּם וְלֹא רָצָה לִישָּׁבַע [וְכוּ׳]. אָמַר רַבִּי חִיָּיא בַּר אַבָּא אָמַר רַבִּי יוֹחָנָן: לֹא ״שִׁילֵּם״ – שִׁילֵּם מַמָּשׁ, אֶלָּא כֵּיוָן שֶׁאָמַר ״הֲרֵינִי מְשַׁלֵּם״, אַף עַל פִּי שֶׁלֹּא שִׁילֵּם.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that if the bailee «paid» the owner «and did not wish to take an oath,» the thief pays the double payment to the bailee. «Rabbi Ḥiyya bar Abba says» that «Rabbi Yoḥanan says:» When the mishna says: If the bailee «paid,» it does «not» mean that he «actually paid. Rather, once» the bailee «said: I hereby» choose to «pay, even if he did not» yet actually «pay,» he acquired the double payment and all other profits."
  }
 ],
